WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.789 --> 00:00:06.940
The world is watching as Russia wages war
on Ukraine.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:10.000
But Russian state media is telling a different
story.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:39.670
Media like the state-owned Russia 24 TV channel
have been following a narrative that President

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:43.000
Vladimir Putin laid out on the morning of the invasion.

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:27.300
The narrative in state media is one clearly
expressed by Putin in his address to the nation.

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:33.080
There is no war going on and it's forbidden
to use the word "war," as you know, you

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:37.940
should speak about a "special operation,"
and this "special operation" is considered

00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:46.850
to be a liberation of Ukrainian people from
the Nazis, from ultranationalists in Kyiv.

00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:53.260
A "special operation" to "liberate"
Ukraine is a cornerstone of the narrative.

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:57.000
Another is Russia's claim that its actions
are pacifism.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:16.400
Pacifism was a very big part of Soviet, and
then Russian, propaganda, even if it was fake

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:17.400
pacifism.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:20.349
War is bad and peace is good.

00:02:20.349 --> 00:02:30.200
So what’s happening now, is that even those
propagandists who are supporting Putin, they

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:34.569
still try to use pacifist narratives.

00:02:34.569 --> 00:02:38.970
According to Russia, it’s the US and NATO
that are threatening peace.

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:45.469
They're trying to present the situation as
if it's not a conflict between Russia and

00:02:45.469 --> 00:02:48.150
Ukraine, it's a conflict between Russia and
America.

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:59.420
This is very important for Putin in this propaganda
campaign, not only to avoid negative information

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:10.109
coming from Ukraine, but also to keep the
idea that the West is conspiring against Russia.

00:03:10.109 --> 00:03:16.510
World War II references and anti-Western rhetoric
are key ingredients fueling what some call

00:03:16.510 --> 00:03:18.169
the Russian propaganda machine.

00:03:18.169 --> 00:03:23.200
But there are signs the engine is stuttering.

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:31.239
Usually our propaganda machine is well-prepared
for all events because the directors of our

00:03:31.239 --> 00:03:36.060
state TV channels and other big state media
are gathering every week on Thursdays in the

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:40.940
Kremlin, and they get instructions about how
to report about this and that.

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:46.879
But no one explained to them that there will
be war in Ukraine.

00:03:46.879 --> 00:03:52.579
Their first narrative, right before
the war started, was that Putin said that

00:03:52.579 --> 00:03:55.769
he is going to return troops back.

00:03:55.769 --> 00:04:04.180
So it's all fake, a "fake Western hysteria"
about a possible war.

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:07.739
Russia is not going to wage a war against
anyone.

00:04:07.739 --> 00:04:12.819
The machine normally works so well, in part
because independent reporting has become increasingly

00:04:12.819 --> 00:04:14.909
scarce in Russia.

00:04:14.909 --> 00:04:21.230
Watchdog Reporters Without Borders ranked
Russia as 150 out of 180 countries for press

00:04:21.230 --> 00:04:28.500
freedom last year, saying that major TV channels
continued to inundate viewers with propaganda

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:32.950
and that vague and selective laws were used
to imprison journalists and bloggers.

00:04:32.950 --> 00:04:40.050
Now it's understandable that it has been done
in advance, in order to [allow] the Kremlin

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:45.250
to control communication almost entirely.

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:48.280
And [that control] will increase.

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:53.320
Once Ukraine was invaded, the Kremlin’s
crackdown on media freedoms only intensified.

00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:59.220
Two of Russia’s most significant remaining
independent media outlets – the Echo of

00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:07.130
Moscow radio station and online TV channel
Dozhd – were forced to close.

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:13.190
During their last moments on air, Dozhd broadcast
a recording of Swan Lake – that state TV

00:05:13.190 --> 00:05:25.270
aired on a loop during the collapse of the
Soviet Union.

00:05:25.270 --> 00:05:34.780
We can tell that independent reporting from
Russia became practically impossible, only

00:05:34.780 --> 00:05:37.400
those outside Russia – they can do it.

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:45.960
The main center of Russian independent media
is abroad, so they will not close all the

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:50.830
information by imprisoning these people who
are still now sitting in Russia.

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:58.240
Russia is not so much separated from the outside
world.

00:05:58.240 --> 00:06:00.840
There is still the internet in the country.

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:05.490
Even though many independent media websites
are banned in Russia, they can still be accessed

00:06:05.490 --> 00:06:11.650
via VPNs – "virtual private networks"
which disguise users’ IP addresses so that

00:06:11.650 --> 00:06:17.230
internet providers – or the government – cannot
see which websites they are visiting.

00:06:17.230 --> 00:06:23.460
Demand has surged in Russia for VPN apps since
war broke out in Ukraine.

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:28.730
Many say the internet, and especially social
media, have become the backbone of the anti-war

00:06:28.730 --> 00:06:34.210
protests that have been taking place in Russia
despite an intense crackdown from police and

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:35.210
lawmakers.

00:06:35.210 --> 00:06:45.740
I think it is actually ironic that in Western
countries over the last years, there has been

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:53.050
a narrative that old-school media checks information
and there is disinformation that goes through

00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:54.800
the social networks.

00:06:54.800 --> 00:07:00.020
In Russia, it’s vice versa – we have disinformation
that’s going through state media and there

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:03.550
is a window for independent media in social
networks.

00:07:03.550 --> 00:07:06.590
So social networks, of course, play a very
important role.

00:07:06.590 --> 00:07:11.770
But even though there is a window for reliable
information on social media – there is also

00:07:11.770 --> 00:07:16.830
a huge amount of disinformation circulating
on the platforms.

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:18.540
Users have to know whom to trust.

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:27.060
But they might not even get the chance – Russia
has now blocked Facebook and Twitter.

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:31.560
Getting independent information on the war
is getting harder by the day.

